{"title":"2025 AIME I Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_grogg007\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by grogg007</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(thorough)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (thorough)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Solution_4_but_different_approach)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Solution 4 but different approach)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_-_Base_Divisibility_by_HungryCalculator\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution - Base Divisibility by HungryCalculator</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_(simplest)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Steakmath (simplest)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(Fast!,_Easy,_Beginner-Friendly)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(Fast!, Easy, Beginner-Friendly)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Quick_&amp;_Easy_Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Quick &amp; Easy Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the sum of all integer bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a165998b29eaf075dd56229f02425a336495d40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5873b8d6c2599ce511a4985d55ec7c935a443609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> is a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/f/9ef3304bc3c3f062da02a43d756d409b23a0ccd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97_b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>First do base conversion of both numbers to write them as 9b² + 7b and b² + 7b \n</p><p>Question is asking such that 9b² + 7b/b² + 7b remainder is 0 \nSo just cancel off one b and seperate one b from 9b and write the equation as 8b/(b+7) + 1 \n</p><p>We only need the cases for b where 8b/(b+7) is an integer \n</p><p>Before manually putting in the values of b we observe that the denominator should have a factors of 8 to cancel so the only cases for b are b = 7,21,49 but since b &gt; 9 then the valid cases are b = 21, 49 \nFinal answer is 21+49 = 70\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_grogg007\">Video solution by <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Grogg007\" title=\"User:Grogg007\">grogg007</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by grogg007\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PNBxBvvjbcU\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=PNBxBvvjbcU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28thorough.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(thorough)\">Solution 1 (thorough)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (thorough)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We are tasked with finding the number of integer bases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a165998b29eaf075dd56229f02425a336495d40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/6/886c8d3265315099558e71a3032307d7d847593e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cfrac{9b+7}{b+7}\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"86\" height=\"43\" />. Notice that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/9/2892d2f999456eaba99d20297fb3d79052db249b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cfrac{9b+7}{b+7}=\\cfrac{9b+63-56}{b+7}=\\cfrac{9(b+7)-56}{b+7}=9-\\cfrac{56}{b+7}\\]\" width=\"398\" height=\"40\" />\nso we need only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f131fed532235eb0784dba210aabe64da3494241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cfrac{56}{b+7}\\in\\mathbb{Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"77\" height=\"43\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594806407e1606d6c9d567855102a49c2ce5383e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> is a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThe factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/a/98a4dbee6b102ca44c1606bc1c67965f905db44c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,2,4,7,8,14,28,56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"158\" height=\"17\" />. Of these, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/c/ecc3bad9624f5220dc88898b12040e25efa17fc1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8,14,28,56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"17\" /> produce a positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8ff51ae926807d5760b7023c083d9636a49cfe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=1,7,21,49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. However, we are what are you looking at that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a165998b29eaf075dd56229f02425a336495d40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/3/0335189fb511a66d215fd1849df249b984281733.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=21,49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> are solutions. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/80087767955955f6b217e711e62cfc484deb7d17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$070$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> .\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/b/62b29b4a95f4361934875ac75ddfb7215872293e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b + 7 \\mid 9b + 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> meaning <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68ab99be70e09ae0f70b1efc656be00cee67caa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b + 7 \\mid -56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" /> so taking divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> under bounds to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e0a6654dd56f1798e4bea2e8cc628c838a2322f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 49, 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" /> meaning our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/7685c00516172bb7c643057b8f0b3d9f5e9b43f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+21=\\boxed{070}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"128\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=User:Mathkiddus\" title=\"User:Mathkiddus\">mathkiddus</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5247f1a67d81e98f5d9eb502f582f73553bf7bea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a(b+7)=9b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"137\" height=\"20\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a natural number. Rearranging we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/8/2e8528a8adb57f12e5711585e4d6be00f227207e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a-9)(b+7)=-56$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/6/a165998b29eaf075dd56229f02425a336495d40d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/2/2c26e5355dccff7f3fe7e734c8a4dc2405b0797a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=49,21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/2/342fa4e699e357eb4c4ab8fa0ad171eda32a7bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49+21=\\boxed{070}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"123\" height=\"25\" /> \n</p><p>~[[User:Wrong Again.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7aea596fcf9ba72aadc758db271ede0302708d7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9b+7}{b+7} = n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"89\" height=\"41\" />. Now, we have: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/5/f453907f328127db5cf99bdc9e2ddd4975a76603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{9(b+7)-56}{b+7} = n \\Longrightarrow 9-\\dfrac{56}{b+7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"258\" height=\"42\" />. Now, we can just find the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/9/6392be3c4d257afbc7ed9283bdb8ba630f4ef7e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$56$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />, subtract <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and sum them. Listing them out, we have the only ones that are positive are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/3/543fb269046e76b297cc5cc72b4ea0cf2f34feb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8-1 = 7, 14-7 = 7, 28-7 = 21, 56-7 = 49$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"366\" height=\"17\" />. But, we have this condition: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/f/0cf43a861481b953fb42a09b48df7ea101bb0bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b &gt; 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, so the only ones that work are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/d/b8df01484f0c182f7d6593ce6bd9d0a2d45ffa44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21,49 \\Longrightarrow 21 + 49 = \\boxed{070}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"207\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Solution_4_but_different_approach.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Solution_4_but_different_approach)\">Solution 5 (Solution 4 but different approach)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Solution 4 but different approach)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We want \\( 17_b \\) to divide \\( 97_b \\). Converting to base 10 gives \\( 17_b = b + 7 \\) and \\( 97_b = 9b + 7 \\). The condition is \\( b + 7 \\mid 9b + 7 \\). Subtracting \\( 9(b + 7) \\) from \\( 9b + 7 \\) gives \\( (9b + 7) - 9(b + 7) = -56 \\). So \\( b + 7 \\) must divide 56. Continue as in Solution 4 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a354c82d4f1f2eb146c6fc23ef3f0cedfecda58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{070}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28Similar_to_Solution_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(Similar_to_Solution_3)\">Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (Similar to Solution 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let's convert everything into base 10. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/5873b8d6c2599ce511a4985d55ec7c935a443609.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594806407e1606d6c9d567855102a49c2ce5383e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/4/1344231a83b06d9eeaa71538960a5ca41facfbad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$97_b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> becomes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d78c2b4c29854c42c9ab351f07b74be02d77fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />. Now we solve the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4199a4a88254d791bd608ef8c11043dc19c55c27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k(b+7)=9b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"138\" height=\"20\" />, where k is an integer. Now while it looks like the equation has infinite solutions, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be an positive integer. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/6/0566a0e99ebec25620d813cbbedde7217e929ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=9$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, the equation has no solution, and when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/d/33d4a429f170bfb56731e26105370d9003212ff4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&gt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" /> the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/594806407e1606d6c9d567855102a49c2ce5383e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" /> side is greater than the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56d78c2b4c29854c42c9ab351f07b74be02d77fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b+7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"16\" />, leading to only negative solutions. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/6/a06b4294709760407e897dc1064e2259f368d2a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k\\le0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />, the expression has only negative solutions, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6584cae382840503e8fc39c3365b52dcd2d9b9b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0&lt;k&lt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"15\" />. Now we can solve for values of k by plugging in k as 8, 7, 6, 5... wait 5 has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/9/b090ae94d100efbb1643c712f420c4d626d683b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b&lt;9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, so our only solutions of b are 21 and 49! (that is not a factorial.) Therefore, our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a354c82d4f1f2eb146c6fc23ef3f0cedfecda58c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{070}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Namish Dour\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1 by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=J-0BapU4Yuk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_-_Base_Divisibility_by_HungryCalculator\">Video Solution - Base Divisibility by HungryCalculator</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution - Base Divisibility by HungryCalculator\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TLq1JaQq_7g\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TLq1JaQq_7g</a>\n</p><p>~HungryCalculator\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_.28simplest.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Steakmath_(simplest)\">Video Solution by Steakmath (simplest)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Steakmath (simplest)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Qi8EjzfoLUU\">https://youtu.be/Qi8EjzfoLUU</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28Fast.21.2C_Easy.2C_Beginner-Friendly.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(Fast!,_Easy,_Beginner-Friendly)\">Video Solution(Fast!, Easy, Beginner-Friendly)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(Fast!, Easy, Beginner-Friendly)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S8aakoJToM0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=S8aakoJToM0</a> \n</p><p>~MC\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Mathletes_Corner\">Video Solution by Mathletes Corner</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Mathletes Corner\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fEYpnDxSlk0\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fEYpnDxSlk0</a> \n</p><p>~GP102\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Quick_.26_Easy_Video_Solution\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Quick_&amp;_Easy_Video_Solution\">Quick &amp; Easy Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Quick &amp; Easy Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A-h121roYg8\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=A-h121roYg8</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I\" title=\"2025 AIME I\">2025 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2025 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2025 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/r